            <ArticleTitle>Choledochal cyst with perforation--an unusual presentation. Case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-6; discussion 97</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A unique case of a 22-month-old baby girl with a perforated choledochal cyst, who presented with vague abdominal symptoms but without any jaundice, an acute abdomen and an incidental finding of acholic stools, is described below with a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
